rationale={'role':'Informed AUTHOR rationale after actual original A-FIRST; no own independent D/P/A/M/V decision','writtenAtUTC':datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),'fourLocalDefects':[{'id':'LFP05a','reason':'In the ideal graphite/LFP model, discharge transfers lithium from LiC6 into delithiated positive FePO4, reducing Fe(III) to Fe(II) and yielding LiFePO4. The existing balanced full-cell equation and transport/safety reasoning already model this direction. Correct only the inverted English state label, explicitly state lithiation; no capacity, range or safety claim changes.'},{'id':'Nernst-a338','reason':'Nernst predicts reversible potentials at specified temperature and activities. Loaded terminal voltage additionally involves activation, ohmic and mass-transport losses. Existing whole12a/b and profile already distinguish these; make the two goal descriptions agree with their actual calculational demand without adding a loss-calculation competence. Temperature-dependent E° must be supplied at the chosen T; the existing cases supply298.15K and matchingE°.'},{'id':'SecondaryCells16b','reason':'The original whole BY C12-GA8.10 duty explicitly includes evaluation of possible uses, independent research, source authorship/trustworthiness and quotations. Restore this English assignment while keeping the complete German body and all research/source duties. No new national-course/source-coverage claim.'},{'id':'Aquatic17b','reason':'A test-specific mineralisation/degradate observation concerns fate. It does not establish ecological effects or real exposure. Retain a provisional choice under the declared degradation priority; expressly retain missing aquatic effects/exposure for both X and Y. Fictional figures, cost/water argument, source uncertainty, independent transfer and all original rubric rows remain.'}],'primaryExternalVerification':[{'url':'https://goldbook.iupac.org/terms/view/09068/plain','title':'IUPAC Gold Book: Nernst equation','use':'Own paraphrase only: equilibrium potential depends on temperature and activities; no copied whole official text.'},{'url':'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6906779/','doi':'10.1021/acsomega.9b02694','title':'Lithium Clustering during the Lithiation/Delithiation Process in LiFePO4 Olivine-Structured Materials','use':'Own factual paraphrase only: LiFePO4 is lithiated, FePO4 delithiated; discharge inserts lithium, Fe(III) is reduced to Fe(II). No external figure/text copied.'},{'url':'https://www.lehrplanplus.bayern.de/fachlehrplan/gymnasium/12/chemie/grundlegend','title':'LehrplanPLUS Chemistry12 basic level, wholeC12.8','use':'Same original duty already in exact own source bindings; English parity correction only.'}],'allOldSourceCourseAtomicityHoldsRetained':True,'noImageGeneration':True,'noNativeRebuild':True,'newVotes':0}
